  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_setting_index(records: list, index_col: str) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Setting Index** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_setting_index(records: list, index_col: str) -> dict:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records).set_index(index_col)\n    return {'index_name': str(df.index.name), 'index_values': [str(x) for x in df.index.tolist()], 'remaining_columns': list(df.columns)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
